        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6f9712a1-af98-5668-a448-77664da80851",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chester Dillon\n- Organizations: Georgetown College, Dakota Wesleyan University, Simpson College, Howard College, Samford University, Oshkosh State Normal School, University of Wisconsin–Oshkosh, Jacksonville State Teachers College, Jacksonville State University\n- Places: Homewood, Alabama, Georgetown, Kentucky\n- Roles: Head football coach\n- Topics: College history\n\nFacts:\n- Georgetown College was chartered in 1829.\n- Georgetown College was the first Baptist college west of the Allegheny Mountains.\n- Chester Dillon served as head football coach at Dakota Wesleyan University from 1915 to 1916.\n- Chester Dillon served as head football coach at Simpson College from 1916 to 1917.\n- Chester Dillon served as head football coach at Howard College in Homewood, Alabama, now Samford University, in 1919 and from 1927 to 1928.\n- Chester Dillon served as head football coach at Oshkosh State Normal School, now the University of Wisconsin–Oshkosh, in 1920.\n- Chester Dillon served as head football coach at Georgetown College in Georgetown, Kentucky, from 1929 to 1930.\n- Chester Dillon served as head football coach at Jacksonville State Teachers College, now Jacksonville State University, from 1938 to 1939 and in 1945.",
